DIRECT /home/vittakis/DC3/CoREASInputs/Xi_Sib_Iron_1.3_53.0_232.6_12/
* ==============================================================================
* A GRAND SHOWER SKELETON FOR CORSIKA (particle simulation, no radio)
* ==============================================================================
* Needs a CORSIKA build with the CURVED, SLANT, THIN and SIBYLL options.
* SimpleCoREASShowerInputGenerator.py writes the event keywords (RUNNR, EVTNR,
* NSHOW, SEED, PRMPAR, ERANGE, THETAP, PHIP, THIN, DIRECT) above this skeleton.
* CORSIKA reads the keywords up to EXIT. Lines starting with * are comments,
* and so is the text after the last argument of a keyword.
* Section numbers below refer to the CORSIKA 7.8050 user guide.
*
* Site, as in Example.ZHAireS.Skeleton.inp (Xiaodushan, ground at 1264 m)
* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
OBSLEV 1264.E2                          observation level (cm)
* Magnetic field of the ZHAireS skeleton, 56.482 uT with inclination 61.6 deg:
* BX = 56.482 cos(61.6 deg) to the north, BZ = 56.482 sin(61.6 deg) downwards.
* The declination is not needed: CORSIKA, like AIRES, takes the azimuth from
* magnetic north.
MAGNET 26.8642 49.6843                  BX BZ (uT)
*
* Atmosphere: the 4 GDAS layers of the ZHAireS skeleton (Dunhuang, gdastool)
* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
* Each layer h1-h2 with densities rho1, rho2 is exponential. In CORSIKA form,
* T(h) = a + b exp(-h/c), with c = (h2-h1)/ln(rho1/rho2), b = rho1 c exp(h1/c),
* and a set to make T continuous, starting from the U.S. standard layer that
* ATMOD 0 uses above 100 km. This gives 904.509 g/cm2 at 1264 m (904.508 in the
* .sry files of the ZHAireS showers).
* ATMA: a (g/cm2), ATMB: b (g/cm2), ATMC: c (cm), for layers 1 to 4;
* ATMLAY: lower boundaries of layers 2 to 5 (cm).
ATMOD  0                                atmosphere given by ATMA, ATMB, ATMC, ATMLAY
ATMA   -2.13255642E+02 -1.20983111E+02 6.61902143E-01 3.87502874E-04
ATMB   1.25803213E+03 1.17360151E+03 1.23362534E+03 1.15682347E+03
ATMC   1.06920970E+06 9.58476904E+05 6.94197835E+05 7.10648512E+05
ATMLAY 3.6888E+05 9.3776E+05 2.6300E+06 1.0000E+07
*
* Interactions
* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
SIBYLL T 0                              SIBYLL for the high-energy hadronic interactions
SIBSIG T                                SIBYLL cross-sections
ELMFLG F T                              NKG off, EGS4 on
* Kinetic energy cuts as in the ZHAireS showers (.sry files) for muons (10 MeV),
* electrons and photons (1 MeV). Hadrons at CORSIKA's default 0.3 GeV (AIRES
* cuts mesons at 60 MeV and nucleons at 120 MeV).
ECUTS  0.3 0.01 0.001 0.001             hadrons, muons, electrons, photons (GeV)
* Hadrons and muons: the same thinning level and weight limit as THIN (in the
* event keywords), since AIRES uses one weight limit for all particles.
THINH  1. 1.                            ratios em/hadronic of thinning level and weight limit
*
* Output
* ------------------------------------------------------------------------------
LONGI  T 5. T T                         profile on, 5 g/cm2 slant steps, Gaisser-Hillas fit, .long file
PAROUT F F                              no particle file and no .tab file (no ground particles needed)
EXIT
